This is a CBP ruling I recall: silt fence of woven polypropylene strips with wooden stakes. It was classified as a set, with the essential character given by the fabric, in heading 5407 or 5903 or 6307. For woven fabric of polypropylene strips, the usual heading is 5407.20 (woven fabrics of strip or the like) for synthetic filament. However, the fabric is made up into a pocket silt fence, so it is a made-up article, which points to 6307.90 (other made up articles). I recall rulings classifying silt fence in 6307.90.9889. Pocket silt fence with stakes, as a set put up for retail, would also go to 6307.90.9889 if the textile fabric gives the essential character.

The alternative would be 3926 or 5407.20.0800, but I'll go with the made-up article classification. 6307.90.9889 is "Other made up articles: Other: Other: Other."

{"hts_code": "6307.90.9889", "reason": "The pocket silt fence is a made-up article of woven polypropylene strip fabric, with the wooden stakes included, so the textile gives the set its essential character and it falls under other made up textile articles."}
